version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-16
keywords:
  - quantum learning theory
  - sample complexity
  - incompatible observables
  - joint measurability
  - unsharp measurement
  - POVM
  - semidefinite programming
  - anticommuting Pauli operators
  - randomized measurements
  - readout error mitigation
  - Qiskit
abstract: >-
  Reproducible Python code for "The Copy Cost of Incompatibility". It computes
  joint-measurability thresholds by semidefinite programming, runs Monte Carlo
  experiments on the copy (sample) complexity of learning with incompatible quantum
  observables (anticommuting Pauli blocks and qubit pairs), and simulates the
  randomized-basis implementation of joint unsharp measurements on Qiskit Aer with a
  device-derived noise model and readout calibration.
